{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_plans_project_state_project_state", "label": "PROJECT_STATE.md \u2014 active-state source of truth", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L1-L435", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_stage_8_in_progress", "label": "Stage 8 in progress (deploy & field-proven)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L3-L41", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gated on credentials Ivan supplies: Singapore project, hosting account, RESEND_API_KEY + verified domain, Turnstile keys, privacy-notice sign-off, CRON_SECRET placement. Everything up to the CI-green replay and env matrix is doable without them."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_seoul_migration_behind", "label": "Seoul one migration behind breaks the email loop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L10", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "20260806000200_email_log_origin is not applied on Seoul while lib/email/eventEmails.ts selects and inserts `origin` unconditionally \u2014 every reminder and survey fails with 42703 against the live database, loudly (rule 12 holds) but for every recipient. handoff_08082026 called Seoul '2 behind \u2014 deliberate'; it is 1 behind and the consequence was never assessed."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_organisation_body_authorisations_empty", "label": "organisation_body_authorisations has zero rows on Seoul", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L12", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "18 Seoul events carry an accrediting_body_id but the authorisation table is empty, so set_event_cpd_config() refuses every event. DEFERRED 57's claim that the migration 'backfilled from reality' is false on Seoul; cause unresolved (backfill no-op'd, or rows removed after)."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_scheduler_has_no_trigger", "label": "The scheduler has no trigger", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "vercel.json was reverted in 72cda80 and no pg_cron job was ever created, so nothing fires /api/cron/dispatch. Setting CRON_SECRET does not make it run: a successful manual invocation proves the endpoint works, not that anything is scheduled, and there is no 'last run at' anywhere. Vercel Hobby caps crons at one run per day, which misses every 60-min reminder window."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_orchestrator_hardening", "label": "Orchestrator hardening (migration 20260805000000)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L32-L36", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Makes a `failed` send retryable \u2014 previously ANY existing email_log row caused 23505 \u2192 skip, so one transient provider error lost that recipient's mail permanently and reported it as `skipped`, which renders 'already sent'. Adds a 3-attempt cap, selectDue ordered by soonest-closing window, readRecipients no longer collapsing a query failure into an empty roster, idempotencyKey on every Resend send, and test:rls finally collecting tests/cron (which had run under no gate at all)."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_control_one_layer_above_the_write", "label": "'A control one layer above where the write happens'", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L21-L23, L34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The repo's recurring defect class, six recorded instances. Examples: the DEFERRED-56 gate read events.organisation_id which authenticated could write (bypassable in two statements); mark_attended minted permanent credit on a cancelled registration because the July guard was vacuous on both paths; the retry cap sat in the shared send core and silently disabled the operator's manual re-send for exactly the recipients needing rescue."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_q32_frontend_decisions", "label": "Q32 \u2014 five frontend calls locked against rendered specimens", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "#0070F3 as a fill-only role with a new --primary-ink (#1C3C94) for the 27 ink sites; strict \u00a77a upheld; the Live pill's 3.28:1 AA failure closed at 7.21:1; wordmark on all four shells via one BrandMark; and the audience boundary made a rule \u2014 the sidebar's Events row removed because it pointed at the attendee directory."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_ci_replay_from_zero", "label": "CI replay-from-zero green (d60b596)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L7", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Root cause was default privileges differing by creating role (postgres got Dxtm, no DML), fixed in the first migration. scripts/ci/replay-and-verify.sh exits 0, which unblocks the Singapore precondition."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_cpd_pivot", "label": "CPD platform pivot (2026-07-03)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L51-L55", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eventar pivoted from internal workshop manager to a CPD/CME/CE event + credit platform (HK launch, HKCP first accrediting body). Decisions Log Q20 reverses Q6.3 single-org and supersedes Q5 magic-link-only staff auth."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_d1_config_hash_fork", "label": "D.1 config-hash fork (pinned-in-hash vs chained-version-table)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L387", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Highest-value open decision \u2014 determines whether canonical serialization sits on the ledger's hot write path. Lean: chained-version-table. Re-entry: a real body relationship or the 3b review. Nothing config-referencing gets built into credit_ledger before it is decided."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_evaluator_versioning_gap", "label": "Evaluator-versioning gap", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L388", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Verdict reproducibility needs the evaluator (code) versioned, not just the inputs (rows + config). Named, deferred to first verdict computation."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_kms_signing_vs_rfc_3161", "label": "KMS-signing vs RFC 3161 timestamping", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L389", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "RFC 3161 TSA is the deferred anchor on record; KMS-signing was never a logged decision and reverts to undecided."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_carried_forward_considerations", "label": "Carried-forward considerations", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L329-L350", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Things to hold in mind during the active build but NOT act on now \u2014 rule 13's mechanism for expanding the mental model without redirecting the action."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_dev_email_stub_removal_protocol", "label": "devEmailStub removal protocol", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L342", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Spans three call sites (registerForEvent plus the two email actions). Removal only once RESEND_API_KEY is set AND a smoke registration confirms the real path; until then all sends log to console."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_migration_drift_row_was_false", "label": "The migration-drift deploy gate was FALSE for weeks", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L340", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The row claimed drift was 'back', naming two migrations as remote-only. Both local files exist, and a full local\u2194Seoul diff on 2026-08-09 showed zero migrations on Seoul without a local file. The only real divergence runs the other way. CLAUDE.md said the opposite the whole time and was right."}, {"id": "docs_plans_project_state_phase_ledger", "label": "Phase ledger (compressed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L403-L425", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_plans_project_state_project_state", "target": "docs_plans_project_state_stage_8_in_progress", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_project_state_stage_8_in_progress", "target": "docs_plans_stages_stage_8", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/plans/PROJECT_STATE.md", "source_location": "L3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_plans_project_state_project_state", "target": "docs_plans_stages_stages_md", "relation": "cites", "